<article class="env-lemma" id="0AJH">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AJH">Lemma <span data-tag="0AJH">87.19.5</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $Y$ be an affine formal algebraic space over $S$. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a map of sheaves on $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$ which is representable by algebraic spaces. Then $X$ is a formal algebraic space. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Write $Y = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits Y_\lambda $ as in Definition <a href="/tag/0AI7" data-tag="0AI7">87.9.1</a>. For each $\lambda $ the fibre product $X \times _ Y Y_\lambda $ is an algebraic space. Hence $X = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits X \times _ Y Y_\lambda $ is a formal algebraic space by Lemma <a href="/tag/0AIU" data-tag="0AIU">87.13.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>